					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/arcamiel" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5554157); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5554157&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606678666" alt="Arcamiel" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5554157)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/arcamiel" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5554157); return false;" >Arcamiel</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606678098 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Nov 2020 19:28</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13888144/dissociative-somnia-phenomenon">Dissociative Somnia Phenomenon</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831524">
									

<p><strong>Seeking greenlight:</strong> YES</p>
<p><strong>Page type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator pitch:</strong><br />
An event in which an individual, usually that suffers from night terrors, will experience a dissociative episode(out of body experience) by &quot;dreaming&quot; about dying or killing. The dreams represent with precision the death of a person close to them, who will die within the next few weeks. Attempts to prevent this fate will often result in catastrophic outcomes.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong><br />
The Inevitability of death and acceptance of loss.</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong><br />
It's the classic &quot;how would you react if you knew someone that you like is going to die?&quot;. I believe this concept to be interesting enough for the small intended size of the article.</p>
<p><strong>Additional notes:</strong><br />
I'm not a hundred percent sure there isn't anything like this on the site already. I've looked around and found nothing that's close, but if there is, please, feel free to warn me.</p>

							</div>

								
					
