																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13887895/complete-desolation">Complete Desolation</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831523">
									

<p>The obvious problem you have is that it's based on a tac-nuke; while it's always fun to go into what a tac-nuke can do, they are just unlikely to target something small enough to be taken out with one. Upgrading it just creates bigger problems. You'd do better with an epidemic or invasion, which have been known to take out towns.</p>
<p>It would also be harder to keep the city out of the news.</p>
<p>It is worth noting that experimentation would be able to determine if he is truly schizophrenic or is actually talking to ghosts; The Foundation would be able to determine that. If he truly is talking to ghosts, then The Foundation would have specialists that would love to talk to him. If he's merely schizophrenic, The Foundation getting him help would make for some interesting debates similar to whether or not he could leave the town.</p>
<p>Otherwise, an excellent start. It should be interesting to see where this goes.</p>

							</div>

								
					
